CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772483663
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/22
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Commons select committee on defence
OL,6, has said the Gurkhas should continue
OL,7, to be part of the British Army.
OL,9,FThe Ministry of Defence is reviewing
OL,10,Ftheir future because three of the
OL,11,FArmy's five Gurkha battalions are
OL,12,Fbased in Hong Kong - which will be
OL,13,Fhanded back to China in 1997.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FBut the MPs said they had decided the
OL,16,FGurkhas were good value for money.
OL,18,FThey added that the Gurkhas could help
OL,19,Ffill the gap caused by a shortage of
OL,20,Fschool-leavers in Britain.
OL,23,T]CFrom 02-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
